Manage cluster

Usage:
  bootwright cluster [command]

Available Commands:
  exec        Print a command access descriptor for independent operator execution; do not launch a client or connect (unavailable)
  info        Show cluster details and static access applicability (unavailable)
  kubeconfig  Export raw sensitive kubeconfig bytes to standard output
  kubectl     Print a kubectl access descriptor for independent operator execution; do not launch a client or connect (unavailable)
  list        List container and storage clusters (unavailable)
  oc          Print an oc access descriptor for independent operator execution; do not launch a client or connect (unavailable)
  rsh         Print an SSH access descriptor for independent operator execution; do not launch a client or connect (unavailable)

Global Flags:
      --context string             Select a context (default: current context)
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines

Use "bootwright cluster [command] --help" for more information about a command.
